    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17170" root="روى" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُوَآءٌ</span></b>  [for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُؤَآءٌ</span>, (see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِئْىٌ</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رأى</span>,) or of the
measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُعَالٌ</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الرِّىُّ</span>, (see Har p. 24,)] <i>i. q.</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنْظَرٌ</span> [as meaning <i>A pleasing,</i> or <i>goodly, aspect;</i>
or <i>beauty of aspect</i>]: so in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ لَهُ رُوَآءٌ</span>
[<i>A man having a pleasing,</i> or <i>goodly, aspect</i>]. (S.)

